# close_on_restart.pdl - extra processes that `button.sh restart | run | reset | quit` must close, read by close_listed.sh.
# Why a list: restart's own sweep (ops/crypt_autostart.c) only knows the taskbar, tp_desktop_window and the open-entity registry, so a window that is just a
# khtpm_core_render process (the hotbar, board windows) survived a restart and the NEW one never showed (owner report 2026-10-06). Add a row to cover any window or helper.
#   CLOSE | <name> | <substring of the process command line> | <optional relaunch command, run from the house root>
# The relaunch command runs only with `close_listed.sh <house> --relaunch` (the taskbar's "$.restart" = run_khtpm_strip.sh new), and only for a row whose process WAS running, so a window
# you closed yourself stays closed. quit / reset / button.sh run do not relaunch (run starts the autostart rows itself).
# A process is closed only if its command line contains BOTH the substring AND this house's root path (so another checkout's windows are never touched).
# Substrings must be specific: a match is TERMed, then KILLed after 1 s. Never write a pattern that could match a shell or this script's own command line.
CLOSE | hotbar-desk window  | @.apps/hotbar-hq/hotbar-desk.xhtpm | sh @.apps/hotbar-hq/boot.sh
CLOSE | hotbar manager      | @.apps/hotbar-hq/ops/+x/hotbar_manager.+x
CLOSE | board windows       | @.apps/board-hq/board-
CLOSE | board manager       | @.apps/board-hq/ops/+x/board_vars_op.+x
